\
### `bootstrap_distributions.png`\
- **File type:** PNG  \
- **Description:** Histogram comparing naive and block bootstrap distributions for Earth circumference. Shaded regions represent bootstrap distributions, dashed lines indicate 95% confidence intervals, solid line shows mean estimate, and a thicker dashed line marks the true circumference (40,030 km).  \
\
### `earth_circumference_bootstrap.R`\
- **Final output variables:**\
  - `circ_estimate` \'96 Estimated Earth circumference for each observation  \
  - `theta_ithaca` \'96 Angle computed from Ithaca measurements  \
  - `theta_kingston` \'96 Angle computed from Kingston measurements  \
  - `delta_theta` \'96 Absolute angular difference  \
  - `boot_naive` \'96 Naive bootstrap object  \
  - `boot_block` \'96 Block bootstrap object  \
- **Bootstrap CI variables (computed for plotting):**\
  - `naive_ci`  \
